  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria Malnutrition Crisis 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria is facing the worst malnutrition crisis in recent decades.&#xa0;
Over 5.44M infants under 5 are malnourished in the North-East &amp; North-West of Nigeria, with 1.76M being severely malnourished and 3.67M moderately malnourished. Over 787&#x2019;000 pregnant or lactating women are acutely malnourished in need of urgent treatment; and 84 out of 133 local government areas (63%) are classified as either IPC-AMN phase 3 (serious) or phase 4 (critical), with remaining 47 LGAs at alert stage.
The IFRC emergency appeal being launched will build on and expand the Nigerian Red Cross Society&apos;s response in the North-East, North-Central and North-West; contributing to prevention and improvement of acute malnutrition (GAM) in the immediate and medium-term, in the most affected communities.</narrative>
  </description>
